course: dictionary
lesson: 11950
title: Cardamom, a spice with a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cardamom is a spice, and you can work out what it is from the words around it. «Mum added a pinch of cardamom to the rice.» A pinch is a tiny amount, and you add things to rice when you cook, so cardamom must be something you put in food.
explain: «The cardamom pods were small, green and shiny.» Pods are the cases that hold seeds. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Cardamom is a seed pod, so the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Traders carried cardamom along the spice routes, long journeys by camel and ship.» Spice routes are trade paths, and traders carry goods on them. Cardamom was one of the spices people bought and sold, so it was valuable.
fact: Cardamom is a sweet, strongly scented spice.
fact: Cardamom comes from the small green or black seed pods of a plant in the ginger family.
fact: The cardamom plant is tall and tropical, and mostly grows in India, Sri Lanka and Guatemala.
fact: Cardamom flavours curries, rice, Indian sweets, chai tea, Scandinavian buns and Arabic coffee.
fact: Useful phrases are cardamom pods, ground cardamom and a pinch of cardamom.
exercise: «Mum put a pinch of cardamom into the rice.» What is cardamom here? | A large green vegetable | A kind of bread roll | *A sweet, strongly scented spice | A type of cold drink
exercise: Where does cardamom grow, according to the lesson? | *India | Canada | Egypt | Iceland
exercise: «The cardamom pods were small, green and shiny.» What are the cardamom pods? | Tiny fish from the sea | *The small seed pods of a plant | Dried leaves from a tea bush | Pieces of bread
test: «Grandma baked cardamom buns for the class, and the kitchen smelled wonderful.» What does the smell tell you about cardamom? | It is cold and wet | *It is strongly scented | It has no smell at all | It is smelly and unpleasant
test: Which phrase means cardamom that has been crushed into powder? | spice routes | *ground cardamom | cardamom pods | a pinch of cardamom
exam: Mia says, «Cardamom is a plant, so it must be a flower.» Which answer is correct? | *Not quite: the spice comes from the seed pods of the plant, which is in the ginger family | Yes, because all spices are flowers | No, because it is a kind of cloud | Yes, because it grows in gardens in England
